by Spomky at 2026-09-28T17:48:10Z

Hi,

Indeed the bug is real. But the key sets are indexed by the issuer the provider announces which is the value an attacker controls. A provider can impersonate a peer by announcing that peer's issuer in its own discovery document.

The right check is the one from [OIDC Discovery §4.3](https://openid.net/specs/openid-connect-discovery-1_0.html#ProviderConfigurationValidation): the announced issuer must match the issuer the discovery URL was built from.

