Thank you both. I pushed an update: with a single discovery endpoint, nothing changes anymore (same key set, same cache entry, the announced issuer isn't checked), so Entra's `common` metadata, a missing `issuer` or a trailing slash keep working on 7.4.
With several endpoints, keys are bound to the issuer each document announces, and an issuer announced by two documents is refused. That closes the case @Spomky described without §4.3: the provider that holds A's key also serves A's document, so both cases need the same attacker IMHO.
A §4.3 check behind an option would be a new feature: PR welcome on 8.2 :)

